Most people jump straight to level 3 (staring at TensorBoard). But 80% of AI bugs live at levels 1 and 2.



The GPU math you suspected is not the bottleneck; the profiler shows the step spending most of its wall time inside the DataLoader.
Each bar is cumulative time in a call, stacked on its caller, so the widest tower marks the function to fix, here by adding loader workers and pinned memory instead of optimizing the model.


